    "platform": "senate.ca.gov district Drupal sites",
    "verified": "2026-07-25",
    "notes": "Full 40-seat chamber, all 40 verified collecting on 2026-07-25. The chamber is split across two hostnames: the 30 Democratic members sit on sdNN.senate.ca.gov, the 10 Republican members are hosted by the caucus on srNN.senate.ca.gov. senate.ca.gov/senators publishes the composition as 30 Democrats / 10 Republicans, which matches that split exactly, so party here is taken from the caucus host. Districts 1, 4, 6, 12, 19, 23, 32, 36, 37 and 40 are the srNN ones; sdNN requests for those districts fail, redirect to an unrelated district, or land on the chamber homepage, which is what made an sdNN-only sweep look like dead sites. Listing paths vary by member and are pinned per row rather than derived: /press-releases, /newsroom/press-releases, /news/press-releases, and /news. Detail URLs also vary -- sdNN members link to /news/<slug> (older sites: /news/press-release/<slug>) and srNN members link to /content/<slug>; the extractor accepts all three. 'In the News' and 'In the Media' listings exist on many of these sites and are deliberately not seeded -- they are third-party clippings, which are out of scope. Not yet seeded but present on several sdNN sites: /news/op-eds and /news/newsletters silos, which are in scope and would need their own pass."
  },
